1. (Currently amended) A system, comprising:
a processor node comprising a processor and a network interface;
a plurality of memory nodes, wherein each memory node comprises a memory and a network interface;
a communication network configured to interconnect said processor node and said plurality of memory nodes via said network interfaces according to a network topology, wherein each of said memory nodes is removed from said processor node by a respective number of network hops according to said network topology;
wherein said processor node is configured to:
broadcast a memory request message comprising a unique identifier of a given memory request, a requested memory size, and __a time-to-live value__ to a subset of said plurality of memory nodes;
send a confirmation message comprising the unique identifier to a particular one of the subset of memory nodes in response to receiving a reservation acknowledgment message from said particular one of the memory nodes __within a time period determined by said time-to-live value__;
and access memory on the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving a commit message from the particular one of the memory nodes indicating that the memory has been allocated for the given memory request __and that the memory has been committed to the given memory request for a duration based on said time-to-live value__.

2. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the processor node is further configured to create a reservation structure for the given memory request comprising the unique identifier, a timeout value __derived from said time-to-live value__, and __a state indicator tracking the reservation lifecycle__, and wherein if a timer reaches the timeout value before a reply message is received in response to a given message being sent by the processor node, the processor node is further configured to re-send the given message __or cancel the reservation based on said state indicator__.

3. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is configured to reserve a portion of memory at least as large as the requested memory size and to send a reservation acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier __and a reservation duration based on said time-to-live value__ to the processor node in response to receiving the given memory request if the given memory request may be satisfied by the particular one of the memory nodes.

4. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to create a reservation structure for the given memory request comprising the unique identifier, a timeout value __derived from said time-to-live value included in the memory request message__, and __a state indicator tracking the reservation lifecycle__, and wherein if a timer reaches the timeout value before a reply message is received in response to a given message being sent by the particular one of the memory nodes, the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to re-send the given message __or release the reservation based on said state indicator__.

5. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to send a commit message comprising the unique identifier __and a commitment duration based on said time-to-live value__ to the processor node in response to receiving the confirmation message from the processor node.

6. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to send a read acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving a read request message comprising the unique identifier __and a read operation identifier__ from the processor node subsequent to receiving the confirmation message, and wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to send a write acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving a write request message comprising the unique identifier __and a write operation identifier__ from the processor node subsequent to receiving the confirmation message.

7. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the processor node is further configured to send a reject message comprising the unique identifier __and a rejection reason__ to the particular one of the memory nodes to indicate that it no longer requires access to the memory allocated for the given memory request.

8. (Currently amended) The system of claim 7, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to free the memory allocated for the given memory request and to send a reject acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier __and a confirmation of memory release__ to the processor node in response to receiving the reject message from the processor node.

9. (Currently amended) The system of claim 8, wherein the processor node is further configured to send a reject confirmation message comprising the unique identifier __and a timestamp of the rejection completion__ to the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving the reject acknowledgement message from the particular one of the memory nodes.

10. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein each memory node of said subset is removed from said processor node by no more than a given number of network hops; and wherein if no memory node of said subset indicates that it can satisfy the given memory request __within a time period determined by said time-to-live value__, the processor node is further configured to increase said given number of network hops and to broadcast the memory request message to a second subset of said plurality of memory nodes, wherein each memory node of said second subset is removed from said processor node by no more than said increased given number of network hops.

11. (Currently amended) The system of claim 10, wherein if no memory node of said second subset indicates that it can satisfy the given memory request __within the time period determined by said time-to-live value__, the processor node is further configured to continue to increase said given number of network hops and to broadcast the memory request message to a corresponding subset of said plurality of memory nodes, wherein each memory node of said corresponding subset is removed from said processor node by no more than said increased given number of network hops, until at least one of the following occurs: one or more of said plurality of memory nodes indicates that it can satisfy the given memory request in response to receiving the given memory request, said processor node has broadcast the memory request message to each of said plurality of memory nodes, or a time-out condition has been met __based on said time-to-live value__.

